From 9bc16a7659eeae2a0ac938a10dab4234308cef20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 23:22:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Honda: add ACURA_RLX_HYBRID as a regular Nidec platform

With the steer bus bridged onto the powertrain bus by the
hondaRlxForwarder panda, the RLX no longer needs any multi-bus handling:
STEER_STATUS and CAR_SPEED are read from the pt bus and STEERING_CONTROL
and LKAS_HUD are sent on the pt bus like any other Nidec car. The only
remaining exception is that the stock LKAS camera's LKAS_HUD is not
visible on the camera bus, so carFaultedNonCritical only uses ACC_PROBLEM.

Platform specs, fingerprints, lateral tuning and torque data are carried
over from the rlx-step21 branch.

Co-authored-by: mliza <mliza@umass.edu>
